<title>COLOMBIA: COLOMBIA INCREASES INTERNAL COFFEE PRICE 12.3 PCT.</title>
<headline>COLOMBIA INCREASES INTERNAL COFFEE PRICE 12.3 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's National Coffee Growers' Federation raised Friday the internal price of coffee 12.3 percent to 358,125 pesos per 125-kg load.</p>
<p>The increase was based on an average trading price of $2.11 in international markets. Since January, Colombia's domestic coffee price has been fixed weekly on a sliding scale in order permit growers to take advantage of international price fluctuations. Last week's price for a 125-kg load was 318,875 pesos.</p>
<p>((--Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
